== Notes ==
* {{i|Little Horn}} or {{i|Euthanasia}} can kill the maggot projectile.
* {{i|Friendly Ball}} can be used on the maggot projectile.

== Damage Scaling ==
Damage scaling is a mechanic introduced in [[The Binding of Isaac: Afterbirth]] to provide a more challenging experience to players, enabling ''some'' enemies to retaliate against high damage attacks by deploying an "armor" of a sort to greatly reduce the amount of damage taken. Further details and an in-depth explanation may be found [[Damage Scaling|here]].

== Trivia ==
* Ultra Pestilence, like the other Ultra Harbingers is an upgraded version of its regular counterpart, {{e|Pestilence}}.
* Upon death, Ultra Pestilence explodes into {{e|Small Maggot}}s that rain down harmlessly into the lava.
* Ultra Pestilence is the only Ultra Harbinger with less than 2000 health, instead having 1800.
** However, the Ultra Pestilence Fly Ball he summons (which has 200 HP) equates his total health to 2000.

